OL,3,AWill self-flying planes transform the
OL,4,Askies?
OL,5,
OL,6,FOver an alfalfa field in California's
OL,7,FSan Joaquin Valley, a small
OL,8,Fcrop-spraying plane is flying scarily
OL,9,Flow to the ground. There's little risk
OL,10,Fto humans though, as the plane is
OL,11,Fpilot-free.
OL,13,F"We can actually go lower than a human
OL,14,Fpilot can," says Russ Marotzke, as the
OL,15,Faircraft skims over the crop.
OL,17,FFlying lower means less spray drift and
OL,18,Ftherefore less chemicals are needed
OL,19,Fthan in conventional manned
OL,20,Fcrop-dusting, he says.
OL,23,APub: 01-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
